**assistant**:
> `Hmisc` masks `dplyr::summarize()`. Thus `across()` is being passed to `Hmisc::summarize()`, outside a dplyr data mask.
> 
> Replace every unqualified `summarize(` in the script with `dplyr::summarise(` (or `dplyr::summarize(`).
> 
> For example, in `output$timeseries` change all three aggregations to:
> 
> ```r
> subdf <- df %>%
>   dplyr::filter(scenario == state$scenario, measure == state$measure) %>%
>   dplyr::group_by(year) %>%
>   dplyr::summarise(
>     mu = Hmisc::wtd.mean(mu, popsum),
>     ci05 = Hmisc::wtd.mean(ci05, popsum),
>     ci95 = Hmisc::wtd.mean(ci95, popsum),
>     .groups = "drop"
>   )
> ```
> 
> ```r
> subdf <- df %>%
>   dplyr::filter(scenario == state$scenario, measure == state$measure) %>%
>   dplyr::group_by(year) %>%
>   dplyr::summarise(
>     dplyr::across(c(mu, ci05, ci95), mean),
>     .groups = "drop"
>   )
> ```
> 
> ```r
> subdf <- df %>%
>   dplyr::filter(scenario == state$scenario, measure == state$measure) %>%
>   dplyr::group_by(year) %>%
>   dplyr::summarise(
>     dplyr::across(c(mu, ci05, ci95), sum),
>     .groups = "drop"
>   )
> ```
> 
> Also change every `summarize(...)` in `get.adaptgraph()` and `get.adaptgraph.with.prev()` to `dplyr::summarise(...)`.
> 
> The second error is likely from this block:
> 
> ```r
> session$onFlushed(function() {
>   state <- map.state()
>   ...
> }, once = TRUE)
> ```
> 
> A flush callback is not necessarily a reactive consumer. Capture `state` *before* registering the callback:
> 
> ```r
> state <- map.state()
> 
> session$onFlushed(function() {
>   session$sendCustomMessage(
>     "updatePolygonStyles",
>     make_map_payload(
>       state$channel, state$scenario,
>       state$measure, state$year, state$quant
>     )
>   )
> }, once = TRUE)
> ```
> 
> More generally, since you load `Hmisc`, use explicit namespaces for the contested verbs throughout:
> 
> ```r
> dplyr::filter()
> dplyr::select()
> dplyr::mutate()
> dplyr::group_by()
> dplyr::summarise()
> ```
> 
> That will make the app robust to package loading order.
